build/
out/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.spv
CMakeUserPresets.json
package/

# The overnight loop's stop marker, created by hand to ask a running loop to finish.
STOP-LOOP

# A clip's built world, kept beside it so the next run does not rebuild it. Derived from the
# .clip file, hundreds of megabytes, and rebuilt automatically whenever the clip changes — so it
# is exactly the kind of thing that must never be committed.
*.clip.world
*.clip.world.part

renders/

# How long each stage of a load took last run, so the next one can weight its bar by what
# things actually cost here. Per-machine, like the built-world cache beside it.
*.clip.load
build-linux/

# The game's own per-user folder, made wherever it is run from.
#
# `default_root()` falls back to `<working directory>/WorldShaper` when there is no platform
# folder — which is what running the binary from the repository root does — so a run leaves
# settings, a world cache and a shelf of worlds derived from `clips/` sitting in the tree. One
# session committed all seventeen of them with a `git add -A` before noticing (D641).
WorldShaper/
